## 7. BACKEND API (Vercel Serverless, TypeScript)

All routes are under `/api` and handled by `api/[...path].ts` using the router in `server/`. Responses use one consistent envelope:

```json
{ "ok": true, "data": { ... } }
{ "ok": false, "error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "Human-readable message", "details": [ ... ] } }
```
Use correct HTTP status codes (400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 422, 429, 500). Never leak stack traces or secrets. Log server errors with `console.error` and a request id. Validate every body, query and path param with Zod. Share DTO types from `/shared`.

